<!--Post: 911--><!--Time: 1093558467-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST911"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, August 26, 2004 - 3:14 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Colette: it looks like &#34;Junior&#34; to me also, as I posted over at kansas.com&#39;s BTK message board last night.  However, that doesn&#39;t mean that&#39;s actually what it says...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 911-->
<!--Post: 913--><!--Time: 1093564060-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST913"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sandy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sandy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, August 26, 2004 - 4:47 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think that it was a good idea to reverse the picture just in case it was flipped over by the BTK. But because of the blue letter that once looked like the tail end of a N at the top left,I think it should also be done back the way it was in case we can make out some other name. Looking at the crease&#39;s in the shirt at least one letter is covered by that crease and it looks like it is next to a S, the starting letter could also be covered by the arm crease.The decoration on it still looks like a puppy with long ears, and a tiny tongue hanging out.The baby looks like a hispanic adorable 6mo. old baby boy. I believe it is the BTK before some tragedy took place in his live, to turn him into the monster he now is. Parents who mistreat children turn them into the monsters we have today.The word mistreat covers many things ,like not showing them love,ignoreing,yelling instead of talking to them.I see children today not respecting their elders,or anyone for that matter,not even them selves.I am sorry for going into all of this ,but when I look at this baby,I can&#39;t help but wonder what went so wrong in his life ?What can we do to help others from becoming evil monsters ?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 913-->
<!--Post: 924--><!--Time: 1093617043-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST924"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, August 27, 2004 - 7:30 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I thought it said &#34;jumbo&#34; Oo <BR> <BR>Meh, that&#39;s just me though.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 924-->
<!--Post: 925--><!--Time: 1093617206-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST925"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, August 27, 2004 - 7:33 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Picture of Bucky Beaver? Link below pic has the Ipana Toothpaste song. Black Knight is mentioned in the song&#42; <BR><a href="http://www.mouseranch.com/buckybeaver/BuckyBeaver.html" target=_top>http://www.mouseranch.com/buckybeaver/BuckyBeaver. html</a> <BR> <BR>The Ipana song is sung by David Seville who had a 1958 hit “Witch Doctor.” &#40;Wichita&#41; <BR> <a href="http://www.theiceberg.com/artist/590/david_seville.html" target=_top>http://www.theiceberg.com/artist/590/david_seville .html</a> <BR><a href="http://www.imdb.com/name/nm0046564/" target=_top>http://www.imdb.com/name/nm0046564/</a> <BR>He died on January 16, 1972, close in date January 15th to to Otero murder date. His son is a “Junior.” <BR> <BR>The inspiration for “Witch Doctor” was a book by Jan de Hartog called “Duel With the Witch Doctor.” De Hartog was the son of a minister. &#42;Notice the Knights armor on the wall in the Curly Locks pic. <BR><a href="http://www.ongoing-tales.com/SERIALS/oldtime/POETRY/curlylocks.html" target=_top>http://www.ongoing-tales.com/SERIALS/oldtime/POETR Y/curlylocks.html</a> <BR><a href="http://www.imdb.com/name/nm0208831/" target=_top>http://www.imdb.com/name/nm0208831/</a> <BR> <BR>With the enhanced picture &#40;Thanks, Tom&#41;, what I thought looked like elastic ties around the baby’s hands, now look like folds of baby fat. I wonder with the lyrics, if BTK hated obesity. <BR> <BR>“The children pray the preacher preached” <BR>This was left out of the BTK poem. The baby’s hands almost look like folded in prayer. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 925-->
<!--Post: 927--><!--Time: 1093617762-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST927"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, August 27, 2004 - 7:42 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The wording on the sweater almost looks like &#34;Johns&#34; to me.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 927-->
<!--Post: 931--><!--Time: 1093628348-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST931"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, August 27, 2004 - 10:39 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Oh.   I see it now.  It says Junior allright, and Bookworm is right.  It has the Bucky Beaver apperance, but I question to wether or not it is actually Bucky Beaver. <BR> <BR>Everyone seems intent on it being Joseph Otero&#39;s son.  However I know that Junior has been used as a cliche nickname for years.  I wouldn&#39;t be surprised if they sold baby clothes with &#34;junior&#34; on them.  Perhaps this is a picture of another male?  Kevin Bright?  Vicki&#39;s children?  Vian&#39;s Children?  Fox&#39;s children?  &#40;I&#39;m not sure who had children and who didn&#39;t&#41; <BR> <BR>What is the rumored wording that was cut off the picture in the corner?  Does anyone know? <BR> <BR>Plus, is this KSN&#39;s first reported letter from BTK?  How could they know it was from BTK?  BTK usually sends letters to the Eagle and to KAKE.  Strange that the photo would go to them if it is indeed from him.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 931-->
<!--Post: 1020--><!--Time: 1094858606-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1020"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Muskogee<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Muskogee<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, September 10, 2004 - 4:23 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hmmm...looks like BTK invented his own kind of Rorschach test.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1020-->
<!--Post: 1023--><!--Time: 1094879198-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1023"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, September 10, 2004 - 10:06 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Maybe the lettering is a mirror image. I viewed the picture with a mirror &#40;looking in a mirror with the picture behind me&#41; and the lettering looks somewhat like &#34;animal&#34; to me. BTK did use an mirror image in his sketch.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1023-->
<!--Post: 1024--><!--Time: 1094888567-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1024"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Boo<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Boo<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->9-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, September 11, 2004 - 12:42 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->To a fresh pair of eyes, for what it&#39;s worth -- the minute I looked at this pic tonight for the first time -- I pulled out my magnifying glass &amp; I saw a word. I think the last four letters spell &#39;sexy&#39;.  There are a few letters preceding those -- but I think the symbol is either a face of a person or a dog -- w/a tongue sticking out. That symbol is wearing a hat -- and that hat looks like it could also be an &#39;x&#39; to me.  &#40;factor x?&#41; Looks like there is a &#39;y&#39; to the right of that -- and possibly an &#39;se&#39; preceding it.  No idea what the first few letters are.  I guess -- just like a word association or an ink blot test -- we all are bound to see something different.  <BR>Looks like the symbol/words are superimposed on the photo &#40;as another poster has mentioned&#41; -- &amp; I agree.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1024-->
<!--Post: 1044--><!--Time: 1095385108-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1044"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, September 16, 2004 - 6:38 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;The code words for me will be... Bind them, toture them, kill them, B.T.K.&#34; <BR><a href="http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/special_packages/btk/history/8321038.htm" target=_top>http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/special_pack ages/btk/history/8321038.htm</a> <BR> <BR>I wonder if the mispelling of &#34;toture&#34; has anything to do with the picture of the baby. &#34;Toture&#34; has the word &#34;tot&#34; in it, that&#39;s if it was intentionally mispelled.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
